$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1. General Procedure for the Ir-Catalyzed
Amination of Benzamides with Anilines To a screw capped vial with a
spinvane triangular-shaped Teflon stir bar were added benzamide (0.20
mmol), aniline (0.21 mmol), IrCp*(OAc)2 (9.0 mg, 0.02 mmol, 10 mol %),
AgNTf2 (232 mg, 0.60 mmol, 3.0 equiv), Cu(OAc)2 (18.1 mg, 0.10 mmol, 50
mol %) and 1,2-dichloroethane (0.66 mL) under atmospheric conditions. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 24 h, filtered
through a pad of celite and then diluted by adding CH2Cl2 (10 mL)and 3 M
aqueous NH3solution.The two layers were separated, and the aqueous layer
was extracted with CH2Cl2 (10 mLx 3). The combined organic layers were
dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo.And the residue was
purified by chromatography on silica gel (n-hexane/EtOAc or
n-hexane/EtOAc/CH2Cl2 or n-hexane/CH2Cl2) to give the desired product.
N-tert-Buty2-[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenylamino]benzamide(Table 3, 6k)
Colorless solid; yield 72%. m.p. 140-142 °C; 1H NMR(600 MHz, CDCl3) δ9.42
(s, 1H), 7.50 (d, J= 8.3 Hz, 2H), 7.42 (ddd, J= 22.7, 8.2, 1.4 Hz, 2H),
7.31 (ddd, J= 8.6, 7.3, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.22 (d, J= 8.4 Hz, 2H), 6.90 -6.82
(m, 1H), 5.98 (s, 1H), 1.46 (s, 9H).; 13C NMR(150 MHz, CDCl3) δ168.9,
145.2, 143.1, 131.7, 127.6, 126.4(q, J= 3.5Hz), 124.4(q, J= 270.0Hz),
122.8 (q, J= 32.0Hz), 121.8, 119.7, 118.1, 116.8, 51.9, 28.8; IR (cm-1)
2969, 2930, 1642, 1591, 1526, 1325, 1162, 1113, 1067, 748; High
Resolution MS (EI): Calculated for C18H19F3N2O [M]+:336.1449,
Found:336.1452.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, triangular-shaped Teflon capped vial used, ee 98%
