$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Cyclization of
Substituted Amidines using PhIO in HFIP. To a stirred solution of amidine
1c (0.5 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in HFIP (1 mL) was added PhIO (0.5 mmol, 1.0
equiv) at room temperature under air. The progress of the reaction was
monitored by TLC using ethyl acetate and hexane as eluent. After 12 h,
the resulting solution was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 x 10 mL) and,
washed with brine (2 x 5 mL) and water (1 x 5 mL). Drying (Na2SO4) and
evaporation of the solvent gave a residue that was purified on silica gel
column chromatography using n-hexane and ethyl acetate as eluent.
2-Methyl-1-phenyl-1H-benzo[d]imidazole 2s as yellow liquid, yield 72%.
Analytical TLC on silica gel, 3:7 ethyl acetate/hexane Rf = 0.20; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.75 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.59 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H),
7.53 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 7.37 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.28 (t, J = 7.6 Hz,
1H), 7.21 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.13 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 2.51 (s, 3H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 151.5, 142.4, 136.4, 135.9, 129.9, 128.8,
127.0, 122.4, 119.9, 118.8, 110.0, 14.0; FT-IR (KBr) 3056, 2956, 2923,
1672, 1597, 1499, 1457, 1395, 1324, 1287, 1248, 1181, 1016 cm-1. Anal.
Calcd. for C14H12N2: C, 80.74; H, 5.81; N, 13.45. Found: C, 80.83; H,
5.78; N, 13.39.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM under air
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Iodobenzene Catalyzed C-H Amination of N-Substituted Amidines Using
m-Chloroperbenzoic Acid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
