$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM GENERAL PROCEDURE To a solution of 14 mmol of compound 2 and 35 mmol (2.5
eq) of potassium carbonate dissolved in 27 ml of N,N-dimethylformamide, 1
g of MSH is added every quarter of an hour, until all the precursor has
disappeared. The temperatures are indicated in the Table. The mixture is
poured into 500 ml of ice cold water. The precipitate formed is then
filtered, washed with water and dried in a steam room at 100°C. Ethyl
1-amino-4-oxo-1,4-dihydro-3-quinolinecarboxylate (2a), yield 71%. IR
(KBr): 3478, 1710, 1620 cm-1; 1H NMR : δ 1.21 (t, 3H, J= 7 Hz, OCH2CH3),
4.14 (q, 2H, J= 7 Hz, OCH2CH3), 6.51 (s, 2H, NH2), 7.40 (t, 1H, J= 8 Hz,
H-7), 7.74 (t, 1H, J= 7 Hz, H-6), 7.91 (d, 1H, J= 8 Hz, H-8), 8.12 (d,
1H, J= 8 Hz, H-5), 8.54 (s, 1H, H-2) ppm; HRMS : m/z calcd for C12H12N2O3
(M+) 232.2384, found 231.0772.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A convenient procedure for N-amination of 4-oxo-1,4-dihydroquinolines
