$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure: In a dry box, aryl halide
(2.0 mmol), HBPin (512 mg, 4.0 mmol), (Ind)Ir(COD) (16.6 mg, 0.04 mmol, 2
mol%) and dmpe (6.0 mg, 0.04 mmol, 2 mol%) or dppe (15.9 mg, 0.04 mmol, 2
mol%) were transferred into a thick-walled air-free flask equipped with a
magnetic stirring bar. The flask was sealed, removed from the glove box,
and stirred at 150 °C (dmpe) or 100 °C (dppe) until the reaction was
judged complete by GC-FID. The reaction mixture was allowed to cool to
room temperature and subsequently placed under vacuum for 1-2 h. The
thick walled flask was brought into the dry box and anhydrous K3PO4 (594
mg, 2.8 mmol, 1.4 eq), Pd2dba3 (18.3 mg, 0.02 mmol, 1 mol%), P(t-Bu)3
(12.1 mg, 0.06 mmol, 3 mol%) or
2-dicyclohexylphosphino-2’-(N,N-dimethylamino) biphenyl (31.5 mg, 0.08
mmol, 4 mol%) or 2-(dicyclohexylphosphino)biphenyl (28 mg, 0.08 mmol, 4
mol%), amine (2.4-2.6 mmol, 1.2-1.3 eq) and DME (3mL) were added. The
flask was then sealed, removed from the dry box and stirred at 100 °C
until the reaction was judged complete by GC-FID. After completion, the
reaction mixture was extracted three times with ether. The combined
organics were washed with brine followed by water, dried over MgSO4, and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude material was then
subjected to column chromatography. Table 2, Entry 7:
N-Phenyl-3-(α,α,α-trifluoromethyl)-5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-
1,3,2-dioxaborolyl)aniline: The general procedure was applied to
3-chloro-α,α,α-trifluorotoluene (361.0 mg, 2.0 mmol). The borylation step
was carried out neat with HBPin (400.0 mg, 3.1 mmol) and dppe (15.9 mg,
0.04 mmol, 2 mol%) at 100 °C for 4 h. The amination step was then carried
out using 2-dicyclohexylphosphino-2’-(N,N-dimethylamino) biphenyl (31.5
mg, 0.08 mmol, 4 mol%) and aniline (224.0 mg, 2.4 mmol) at 100 °C for 18
h. Column chromatography (hexanes/CH2Cl2 2:3) furnished the desired
product (515.7 mg, 71 %) as a light yellow solid; mp 83-85 °C. 1H NMR
(C6D6, 500 MHz) δ 8.03 (d, J = 0.9 Hz, 1 H), 7.74 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1 H),
7.14-7.13 (m, 1 H), 7.02-6.99 (m, 2 H), 6.84-6.82 (m, 2 H), 6.79-6.76 (m,
1 H), 4.96 (br s, 1 H), 1.06 (s, 12 H). 13C NMR (C6D6, 125 MHz) δ 144.0
(C), 142.2 (C), 131.5 (q, 2JC-F = 32.1 Hz, C), 129.7 (CH), 126.4 (CH),
125.0 (q, 1JC-F = 272 Hz, CF3), 123.3 (q, 3JC-F = 3.6 Hz, CH), 122.3
(CH), 118.9 (CH), 116.3 (q, 3JC-F = 3.6 Hz, CH), 84.2 (C), 24.8 (CH3).
11B NMR (C6D6, 96 Hz) δ 29.9. 19F NMR (C6D6, 282 MHz) δ -62.7. FT-IR
(NaCl) 3397, 3362, 3040, 2980, 2932, 2870, 1595, 1520, 1497, 1520, 1497,
1470, 1447, 1414, 1389, 1331, 1300, 1273, 1240, 1215, 1167, 1142, 1125,
1100, 1080, 1030, 996, 970, 953, 876, 851, 828, 760, 745, 710, 696, 689,
666 cm-1. LRMS (% rel. int.): m/z 363 (100), 348 (5), 344 (4), 281 (5),
277 (11), 263 (45), 242 (5), 216 (14), 193 (9), 174 (7), 167 (9), 85 (9),
77 (13), 59 (10). Anal. Calcd for C19H21BF3NO2: C, 62.83; H, 5.83; N,
3.86. Found: C, 62.65; H, 5.55; N, 3.78. HRMS Cald for: C19H21BF3NO2: M+
363.1617. Found: 363.1607.
