$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2. Procedure of the C-H Amination of Aromatic
Compounds. General Procedure. The anodic oxidation was carried out using
an H-type divided cell (4G glass filter) equipped with an anode
consisting of fine fibers made from carbon felt (Nippon Carbon JF-20-P7,
ca. 160 mg, dried at 300 °C/1 mmHg for 4 hours before use) and a platinum
plate cathode (10 mm × 10 mm). In the anodic chamber was placed a
solution of aromatic compound (0.20 mmol) and pyridine (0.5 mL) in 0.3 M
Bu4NBF4/CH3CN (10.0 mL). In the cathodic chamber were placed
trifluoromethanesulfonic acid (200 μL) and 0.3 M Bu4NBF4/CH3CN (10.0 mL).
The constant current electrolysis (8.0 mA) was carried out at 25 °C with
magnetic stirring. After X F mol-1 of electricity was consumed, the
reaction mixture was transferred to a round-bottom flask and was
evaporated. Then, piperidine (200 μL, 2.0 mmol) and CH3CN (10 mL) were
added to the reaction mixture. The resulting mixture was stirred at 80 °C
for 12 hours. After removal of the solvent under reduced pressure, the
crude product was purified with flash chromatography or preparative GPC.
Electrochemical oxidation (8 mA, 3.0 F mol-1) of anisole (1) and
subsequent treatment with piperidine afforded compound. 4-phenylaniline
(4). Electrochemical oxidation (8 mA, 3.5 F mol-1) of biphenyl (3) and
subsequent treatment with piperidine gave the title compound (24.3 mg,
72%) as white solid.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, electrochemical (3.5 Faraday per mole), regioselective,
constant current=8mA, fibers made from carbon felt used as anode and
platinum plate used as cathode, H-type cell containing solution of
aromatic substrate, pyridine, Bu4NBF4 and acetonitrile placed in anodic
chamber and solution of trifluoromethanesulfonic acid, Bu4NBF4 and
acetonitrile placed in cathodic chamber used, mechanism studied, 0.20
mmol scale
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Electrochemical C-H Amination: Synthesis of Aromatic Primary Amines via
N-Arylpyridinium Ions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Morofuji, Tatsuya; Shimizu, Akihiro; Yoshida, Jun-ichi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2013), 135(13), 5000-5003

