$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the preparation of amino
pyridones Pyridone of general structure I and NaNO2(1.05 mmol/mmol I)
were suspended in CH2Cl2 (25 mL/mmol I) and a balloon filled with oxygen
gas was connected to the flask via a rubber septum. TFA (1.0 mL/mmol I)
was added drop-wise while stirring at rt. The mixture was stirred over
night and then quenched by addition of NaHCO3 (aq, sat). The organic
phase was separated and the aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2. The
combined organic phases were dried over Na2SO4, filtrated and
concentrated under reduced pressure.The crude product was dissolved in
acetic acid (6 mL/mmol I) and Zn (dust) (5.0 mmol/mmol I) was added. The
mixture was stirred at rt 4 h, and was then filtrated through a pad of
Celite and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was dissolved
in CH2Cl2 and washed with NaHCO3(aq, sat). The aqueous phase was
extracted with CH2Cl2 and the combined organic phases were dried over
Na2SO4(s), filtrated and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude
product was purified with silica gel chromatography (heptane:ethyl
acetate 1:1→1:4). Compound 11a and 11b were prepared according the
published procedure.6 Methyl
(3R)-5-amino-4-oxo-6-phenyl-7-[m-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]-1-thia-3a-aza-3-indancarboxylate
(7b): Prepared by following the general procedure, white foam 495mg
(70%). [α]D-106 (c 0.5, CHCl3); IR ν 3474, 3362, 1753, 1642, 1581, 1511,
1439, 1216, 756, 723, 701 cm-1; 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.51 (dd, J =
2.4, 11.6 Hz, 1H), 3.69 (dd, J = 8.4, 11.6 Hz, 1H), 3.88 (s, 3H), 5.73
(dd, J = 2.4, 8.0 Hz, 1H), 6.95-6.99 (m, 1H), 7.16-7.26 (m, 7H), 7.36 (d,
J = 8.4 Hz, 1H); 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 32.0, 53.5, 63.9, 115.0,
122.5, 123.9, 125.2, 127.2, 127.9, 128.5, 128.9 129.6, 130.2, 130.5,
131.1, 131.9, 133.4, 135.1, 138.3, 156.9, 168.6. LCMS m/z = 447 (M+H),
C22H17F3N2O3S requires 446.
