$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: IV-2. General Procedures for the Ru-Catalyzed
Selective C-N Amidation Reaction with Acyl Azides (Scheme 3) To an
oven-dried screw capped vial equipped with a spinvane triangular-shaped
Teflon stirbar were added 2-arylpyiridne (1, 0.2 mmol), acyl azide (2,
0.36 mmol), [RuCl2(p-cymene)]2 (6.1 mg, 5 mol %), AgSbF6 (13.8 mg, 20 mol
%), 2-nitrobenzoic acid (10.0 mg, 30 mol %) and 1,2-dichloroethane (0.5
mL) under atmospheric conditions. The reaction mixture was stirred in a
pre-heated oil bath at 50 °C for 18 h. The reaction was cooled to room
temperature, filtered through a pad of celite and then washed with CH2Cl2
(10 mL x 3). The solvents were removed under reduced pressure and the
crude reaction mixture was purified by silica gel column chromatography
with n-hexane/EtOAc as an eluent. The desired C-N bond forming products
4. N-[5-Methyl-2-(pyridin-2-yl)phenyl]benzamide (Scheme 3, 4b)
4-Methyl-N-[2-(pyridin-2-yl)phenyl]benzamide (4j) White solid. m.p.
146-147 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 13.24 (s, 1H), 8.79 (dd, J = 8.4,
1.3 Hz, 1H), 8.65 (d, J = 3.2 Hz, 1H), 7.92 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 7.85 -
