$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of [Ru(ArNHAaiMe)3](ClO4)2 (IIa): A
mixture of I (0.20 g, 0.23 mmol) and PhNH2 (0.5 ml) was heated on a steam
bath for 4 h. The initial brown color of the mixture gradually became
ink-blue. The mixture was cooled and washed thoroughly with diethyl ether
for several times. Finally, it was purified on a preparative TLC plate
using a 40% chloroform-acetonitrile mixture as the eluent (firstly,
chromatographed and then the solvent was separated and dried). The
intense blue product, thus obtained, was recrystallized from a
toluene-acetonitrile mixture. [Ru(ArNHMeAaiMe)3] (ClO4)2 (IIb), yield
70%. For [Ru(ArNHMeAaiMe)3] (ClO4)2 (C51H51N15Cl2O8Ru) (IIb) anal. calcd,
%: C 54.5; H 3.7. Found, %: C 54.3; H 3.5. FTIR (KBr; ν, cm-1): 3410
ν(N-H), 1620 ν(C=C), 1599 ν(C=N), 1327 ν(N=N), 1190, 1089, 649 ν(ClO4);
1H NMR (CDCl3; δ, ppm): 8.13 (d., 7, 11H), 7.99 (d., 8, 10H), 8.13 (d.,
13, 17H), 7.93 (t., 14, 16H), 1.62 (t., 15-Me), 7.32 (d., 4H), 7.61 (d.,
5H), 1.97 (s., N-Me).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Aromatic ring aminated trischelates of ruthenium(II): Synthesis and
spectral characterization
