$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of [Ru(HL2a)3](ClO4)2 (2a). A
mixture of [Ru(pap)3](ClO4)2 (0.20 g, 0.23 mmol) and PhNH2 (0.5 mL) was
heated on a steam bath for 4 h. The initial brown color of the mixture
gradually became ink-blue. The mixture was cooled and washed thoroughly
with diethyl ether for several times. Finally, it was purified on a
preparative TLC plate using a 40% chloroform-acetonitrile mixture as the
eluent. The product, thus obtained, was recrystallized from a
toluene-acetonitrile mixture. 2c. Yield: 70%. Anal. Calcd for
C54H48N12Cl2O11Ru: C, 53.47; H, 3.99; N, 13.86. Found: C, 53.27; H, 3.88;
N, 13.76. IR (KBr) (ν, cm-1): 3380 ν(N-H), 1590 ν(C=C + C=N), 1295
ν(N=N), 1150, 630 ν(ClO4), abs(solvent CH3CN) [λ max, nm (ε, M-1 cm-1),]
608 (59 430), 498 (40 120), 284 (46 470),
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ruthenium Complexes of 2-[(4-(Arylamino)phenyl)azo]pyridine Formed via
Regioselective Phenyl Ring Amination of Coordinated
2-(Phenylazo)pyridine: Isolation of Products, X-ray Structure, and Redox
and Optical Properties
