$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (Table 4, Entry 1 Product):
3-[(2-methylpyridin-3-yl)oxy]-5-(pyridin-4-ylsulfanyl)pyridin-2-amine:The
starting material (50 mg; 0.149 mmol) was combined with saccharin (30 mg;
0.164 mmol)and slurried in 0.5 mL of CH2Cl2. iPr2NEt was added (0.052 mL;
0.298 mmol) and the resulting solution was cooled to 0-5 °C using an
ice-bath. A solution of tosyl chloride (34 mg ; 0.179 mmol)was prepared
in 0.1 mL CH2Cl2 and added to the reaction flask via syringe over 10 min.
Theresulting mixture was stirred at 0-5 °C for 2 h then allowed to warm
to RT. The reaction mixture was then treated with 0.25 mL of 5N HCl with
stirring. The lower CH2Cl2 layer was removed and the aqueous product
layer heated to 80 °C overnight. Added 0.5 mL of EtOH and then added 1mL
of 2N aq K2PO4 followed by addition of 10 N NaOH until pH=6 by pH paper.
Extracted aqlayer with 1 mL of IPAC then concentrated down to an oil.
Purified via crystallization from 1: 2CH2Cl2 / heptane. (Table 4, Entry 1
Product):
3-[(2-methylpyridin-3-yl)oxy]-5-(pyridin-4-ylsulfanyl)pyridin-2-amine,
(45mg, 97%), conversion 100%, regioisomer ratioa 27.8:1 M.P = 157 °C HRMS
calc for C16H15ON4S 311.0955, found 311.0961 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ
8.37 (dd, J = 4.7, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 8.34 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 2H), 8.02 (d, J =1.8
Hz, 1H), 7.23 (dd, J = 8.1, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.17 (dd, J = 8.1, 4.7 Hz, 1H),
6.88 (d, J = 6.2 Hz, 2H),6.86 (d, J = 1.8 Hz, 1H), 5.22 (bs, 2H), 2.50
(s, 3H). 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3) δ 151.9, 151.0, 150.8, 149.3, 149.3,
149.1, 145.6, 139.5, 128.0, 126.2, 122.4, 119.9, 112.8, 19.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, 27.8:1 mixture of regioisomers obtained
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
