$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure C: Synthesis of indolines
via Pd-catalyzed intramolecular amination of δ -C(sp2)-H bonds (condition
A). A mixture of picolinamide (1.0 mmol, 1.0 eq), Pd(OAc)2 (4.5 mg, 0.02
mmol, 0.02 eq), PhI(OAc)2 (645 mg, 2.0 mmol, 2.0 eq) and toluene (8 mL)
in a 20 mL glass vial (purged with Ar, sealed with PTFE cap) was heated
at 60 °C for 24 hours. The reaction mixture was cooled to rt, and
concentrated in vacuo. The resulting residue was purified by silica gel
flash chromatography to give the cyclized product. Compound 5 was
prepared following the standard procedure C in 95%; Compound 5' was
prepared following the standard procedure C in 3%. 5: 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400
MHz) δ 8.64 (m, 1H), 8.50 (s, 1H), 7.88-7.84 (m, 2H), 7.41-7.26 (m, 3H),
4.45 (t, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H), 3.33 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.5
MHz) δ 154.23, 148.39, 145.03, 137.44, 130.75, 129.86, 128.24, 127.14,
