$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure D: Synthesis of indolines
via Pd-catalyzed intramolecular amination of δ -C(sp2)-H bonds (condition
B). A mixture of picolinamide (1.0 mmol, 1.0 eq), Pd(OAc)2 (1.1 mg, 0.005
mmol, 0.005 eq), PhI(OAc)2 (645 mg, 2.0 mmol, 2.0 eq) and toluene (8 mL)
in a 20 mL glass vial (purged with Ar, sealed with PTFE cap) was heated
at 80 °C for 24 hours. The reaction mixture was cooled to rt, and
concentrated in vacuo. The resulting residue was purified by silica gel
flash chromatography to give the cyclized product. Compound 7 was
prepared following the standard procedure D in 90% yield. Compound 7' was
prepared following the standard procedure D in 6% yield. 7: 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 8.63 (d, J = 4.7 Hz, 1H), 8.31 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 1H),
7.86-7.83 (m, 2H), 7.45-7.39 (m, 2H), 6.98 (s, 1H), 4.40 (t, J = 8.1 Hz,
2H), 3.10 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.5 MHz) δ 166.49,
154.07, 148.08, 143.36, 137.17, 136.89, 133.12, 129.22, 125.25, 124.31,
117.47, 92.93, 49.44, 34.02; HRMS Calcd for C14H12IN2O [M+H+]: 350.9989;
Found: 350.9995. 7': 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 8.55 (d, J = 4.1 Hz, 1H),
8.21 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 7.87 (td, J = 7.7, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.74 (dd, J =
1.0, 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.44-7.41 (m, 1H), 7.06 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 6.98 (t, J
= 8.0 Hz, 1H), 3.64 (q, J = 6.7 Hz, 2H), 3.11 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 2H), 2.37
(s, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.5 MHz) δ 169.74, 164.68, 150.08, 149.16,
148.19, 137.46, 137.39, 134.25, 129.24, 126.29, 123.14, 122.21, 101.58,
38.50, 35.35, 21.06; HRMS Calcd for C16H16IN2O3 [M+H+]: 411.0200; Found:
411.0208.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, capped vial used
