$DATUM General procedure C: Synthesis of indolines via Pd-catalyzed
intramolecular amination of δ -C(sp2)-H bonds (condition A). A mixture of
picolinamide (1.0 mmol, 1.0 eq), Pd(OAc)2 (4.5 mg, 0.02 mmol, 0.02 eq),
PhI(OAc)2 (645 mg, 2.0 mmol, 2.0 eq) and toluene (8 mL) in a 20 mL glass
vial (purged with Ar, sealed with PTFE cap) was heated at 60 °C for 24
hours. The reaction mixture was cooled to rt, and concentrated in vacuo.
The resulting residue was purified by silica gel flash chromatography to
give the cyclized product. Compound 2 was prepared following the standard
procedure C in 88%; Compound 3 was prepared following the standard
procedure C in 6%. 2: 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 8.63 (d, J = 4.4 Hz, 1H),
8.32 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.86-7.82 (m, 2H), 7.38 (s, 1H), 7.27-7.21 (m,
2H), 7.09 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 4.36 (t, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 3.16 (t, J = 8.3
Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.5 MHz) δ 166.01, 154.26, 147.90, 142.99,
137.01, 132.11, 127.18, 124.95, 124.54, 124.24, 123.94, 117.68, 50.39,
28.46; HRMS Calcd for C14H13N2O [M+H+]: 225.1028; Found: 225.1021. 3: 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 8.61 (d, J = 3.5 Hz, 1H), 8.21 (d, J = 6.3 Hz,
1H), 7.85 (m, 2H), 7.37 (s, 1H), 7.26 (s, 1H), 6.81 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 1H),
4.40 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 3.04 (t, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H), 2.28 (s, 3H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 75.5 MHz) δ 168.85, 166.48, 154.56, 148.43, 147.41, 145.46,
137.50, 129.03, 125.56, 124.96, 124.52, 117.76, 115.89, 51.04, 26.36,
21.20; HRMS Calcd for C16H15N2O3 [M+H+]: 283.1077; Found: 283.1084.
