$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure D: Synthesis of indolines
via Pd-catalyzed intramolecular amination of δ -C(sp2)-H bonds (condition
B). A mixture of picolinamide (1.0 mmol, 1.0 eq), Pd(OAc)2 (1.1 mg, 0.005
mmol, 0.005 eq), PhI(OAc)2 (645 mg, 2.0 mmol, 2.0 eq) and toluene (8 mL)
in a 20 mL glass vial (purged with Ar, sealed with PTFE cap) was heated
at 80 °C for 24 hours. The reaction mixture was cooled to rt, and
concentrated in vacuo. The resulting residue was purified by silica gel
flash chromatography to give the cyclized product. Compound 8 was
prepared following the standard procedure D in 82% yield. Compound 8' was
prepared following the standard procedure D in 10% yield. 8: 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 8.62 (d, J = 3.3 Hz, 1H), 8.30 (s, 1H), 7.90- 7.84 (m,
2H), 7.41 (s, 1H), 7.25 (d, J = 5.2 Hz, 1H), 6.98 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 1H),
4.49 (m, 2H), 3.19 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.5 MHz) δ
166.27, 153.44, 148.49, 147.97, 144.89, 137.10, 132.54, 125.40, 125.26,
124.26, 120.81, 116.64, 111.23, 51.21, 28.03; HRMS Calcd for
C15H12F3N2O4S [M+H+]: 373.0464; Found: 373.0474. 8': 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400
MHz) δ 8.62 (d, J = 3.8 Hz, 1H), 8.22 (s, 1H), 7.90- 7.83 (m, 2H), 7.42
(s, 1H), 6.82 (s, 1H), 4.51 (m, 2H), 3.07 (t, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 2.30 (s,
3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.5 MHz) δ 167.90, 166.38, 153.42, 148.78, 148.14,
146.79, 146.09, 137.36, 125.72, 124.96, 124.71, 120.94, 116.68, 111.14,
109.34, 51.27, 25.94, 20.86; HRMS Calcd for C17H14F3N2O6S [M+H+]:
431.0519; Found: 431.0526.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, capped vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Improved Protocol for Indoline Synthesis via Palladium-Catalyzed
Intramolecular C(sp2)-H Amination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
