$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM III-1. Optimization of the Rh-Catalyzed C-C Amidation Reaction (Table 1)
To an oven-dried screw capped vial with a spinvane triangular-shaped
Teflon stirbar were added 2-phenylpyridine (1a, 28.6 µL, 0.2 mmol),
benzoyl azide (2a, 43.7 µL, 0.36 mmol), catalyst, additive, and solvent
(0.5 mL) under atmospheric conditions. The reaction mixture was stirred
in a pre-heated oil bath at the indicated temperature for 18 h. The
reaction was cooled to room temperature, filtered through a pad of celite
and then washed with CH2Cl2 (10 mL x 3). The solvents were removed under
reduced pressure. The crude yield was measured by NMR using
1,1,2,2-tetrachloroethane as an internal standard. Entry: 21 Yielda:
3a:4a: 81:10 N-Phenyl-2-(pyridin-2-yl)benzamide (3a) White solid.
N-[2-(Pyridin-2-yl)phenyl]benzamide (4a) White solid. 3a: m.p. 112-113
°C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.89 (s, 1H), 8.58 (d, J = 4.4 Hz, 1H),
7.72 (dd, J = 17.4, 7.6 Hz, 2H), 7.52 – 7.39 (m, 6H), 7.24 (td, J = 6.2,
5.2, 2.2 Hz, 3H), 7.04 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
167.7, 158.3, 148.7, 138.3, 137.0, 136.3, 130.3, 130.3, 129.3, 128.8,
128.7, 124.2, 124.2, 122.6, 120.0; IR (cm-1) 2922, 2853, 1657, 1590,
1521, 1497, 1439, 1320, 1060, 994; HRMS (FAB+) m/z calcd. for C18H14N2O
[M+H]+: 275.1184, found: 275.1187. 4a: m.p. 113-114 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 13.33 (s, 1H), 8.80 (dd, J = 8.3, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 8.64 (d, J = 4.9
Hz, 1H), 8.03 (dd, J = 7.9, 1.7 Hz, 2H), 7.85 - 7.72 (m, 2H), 7.70 (dd, J
= 7.9, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.56 - 7.40 (m, 4H), 7.25 (ddd, J = 7.1, 4.9, 1.4 Hz,
1H), 7.18 (td, J = 7.6, 1.3 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 165.4,
158.2, 147.2, 138.1, 137.8, 135.7, 131.4, 130.1, 128.7, 128.5, 127.3,
125.4, 123.5, 122.9, 121.9, 121.8; IR (cm-1) 3053, 2923, 1665, 1586,
1472, 1436, 1313, 1242, 752, 694; HRMS (EI+) m/z calcd. for C18H14N2O
[M]+: 274.1106, found: 274.1106.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, alternative preparation shown (for the major product),
optimized on catalyst, additive, solvent and reaction temperature,
optimization study
