$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: IV-1. General Procedures for the Rh-Catalyzed
Selective C-C Amidation Reaction with Acyl Azides (Scheme 2) To an
oven-dried screw capped vial equipped with a spinvane triangular-shaped
Teflon stirbar were added 2-arylpyiridne (1, 0.2 mmol), acyl azide (2,
0.36 mmol), [RhCp*Cl2]2 (4.9 mg, 4 mol %), AgSbF6 (11.0 mg, 16 mol %),
CH3CN (10.5 µL, 100 mol %) and 1,2-dichloroethane (0.5 mL) under
atmospheric conditions. The reaction mixture was stirred in a pre-heated
oil bath at 70 °C for 18 h. The reaction was cooled to room temperature,
filtered through a pad of celite and then washed with CH2Cl2 (10 mL x 3).
The solvents were removed under reduced pressure and the crude reaction
mixture was purified by silica gel column chromatography with
n-hexane/EtOAc or n-hexane/CH2Cl2 as an eluent. The desired C-C bond
forming products 3. 5-Methyl-N-phenyl-2-(pyridin-2-yl)benzamide (3b)
2-(Pyridin-2-yl)-N-(p-tolyl)benzamide (3j) White solid. m.p. 137-138 °C;
1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.70 (s, 1H), 8.58 (d, J = 5.0 Hz, 1H), 7.75
(d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.71 (td, J = 7.8, 1.9 Hz, 1H), 7.52 - 7.40 (m, 4H),
7.30 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.24 - 7.21 (m, 1H), 7.05 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H),
2.28 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.5, 158.3, 148.8, 138.2,
136.9, 136.4, 135.7, 133.8, 130.2, 130.2, 129.3, 129.2, 128.7, 124.2,
122.5, 120.0, 20.9; IR (cm-1) 2921, 2852, 1659, 1591, 1537, 1511, 1425,
1320, 1272, 1112; HRMS (FAB+) m/z calcd. for C19H16N2O [M+H]+: 289.1341,
found: 289.1342.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, crude ratio biarylcarboxamide:N-biaryl amide = 8:1,
products depend on catalyst used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Orthogonal Reactivity of Acyl Azides in C-H Activation: Dichotomy between
C-C and C-N Amidations Based on Catalyst Systems
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Shin, Kwangmin; Ryu, Jaeyune; Chang, Sukbok
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(7), 2022-2025

