$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for C-H amination reactions:
To a stirred solution of organic substrate and [TpmMe,MeFe(CH3CN)3](BF4)2
(1Fe, 5 mol%) in anhydrous CH2Cl2 or CH3CN (4 mL) with 4 Å molecular
sieves was added solid PhI=NTs (0.2 mmol) in one portion at room
temperature under argon. The reaction mixture was stirred for 30 min,
filtered through a plug of silica gel, eluted with ethyl acetate, and
evaporated to dryness. The crude product derived from amination of THF
was analyzed directly by 1H NMR with mesitylene (0.1 mmol) added as an
internal standard to determine the yield. In other cases, the filtrate
was concentrated under vacuum and purified by column chromatography as
already described.
4-methyl-N-(2,4,6-trimethylphenyl)-benzenesulfonamide,yield 81%;
4-methyl-N-(3,5-dimethylbenzyl)benzenesulfonamide, yield 81%.
4-methyl-N-(2,4,6-trimethylphenyl)-benzenesulfonamide: 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3; δ, ppm): 7.61 (2H, d, 8.1 Hz); 7.24 (2H, d, 8.4 Hz); 6.82 (2H, s);
5.98 (1H, s); 2.42 (3H, s); 2.24 (3H, s); 1.99 (6H, s). 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3; δ, ppm): 143.7 (1C); 138.2 (1C); 137.7 (1C); 137.6 (2C); 130.2
(1C); 129.7 (2C); 129.7 (2C); 127.4 (2C); 21.7 (1C); 21.1 (1C); 18.8
(2C). 4-methyl-N-(3,5-dimethylbenzyl)benzenesulfonamide: 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3; δ, ppm): 7.76 (2H, d, 8.1 Hz); 7.31 (2H, d, 8.2 Hz); 6.87 (1H, s);
6.76 (2H, s); 4.70 (1H, t, 5.9 Hz); 4.05 (2H, d, 6.1 Hz); (6H, s); (3H,
s).
