$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Amination Procedure. Diethyl
1-Amino-3-methylpyrrole-2,4-dicarboxylate (3a). Method A. To a solution
of pyrrole 2a (1 mmol) in DMF (2 mL) was added NaH (1.2 mmol), and the
reaction was stirred for 45 min at room temperature. NH2Cl (8 mL, ca.
0.15 M in ether) was added via syringe while maintaining a nitrogen
sparge. The reaction was monitored by HPLC until completion. The reaction
was then quenched with saturated aqueous Na2S2O3, diluted with water, and
extracted into ether. Compound No: 3a. yield 75%. Compound No: 4. yield
25%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative reaction conditions shown, yield depends on the ratio of
agents and pH
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
