$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure D: Synthesis of indolines
via Pd-catalyzed intramolecular amination of δ -C(sp2)-H bonds (condition
B). A mixture of picolinamide (1.0 mmol, 1.0 eq), Pd(OAc)2 (1.1 mg, 0.005
mmol, 0.005 eq), PhI(OAc)2 (645 mg, 2.0 mmol, 2.0 eq) and toluene (8 mL)
in a 20 mL glass vial (purged with Ar, sealed with PTFE cap) was heated
at 80 °C for 24 hours. The reaction mixture was cooled to rt, and
concentrated in vacuo. The resulting residue was purified by silica gel
flash chromatography to give the cyclized product. Compound 11 was
prepared following the standard procedure D in 72% yield. Compound 11'
was prepared following the standard procedure D in 10% yield. 11: 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 8.63 (d, J = 3.5 Hz, 1H), 8.13 (s, 1H), 7.86- 7.82 (m,
2H), 7.48 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H), 7.40-7.30 (m, 4H), 7.10 (d, J = 8.1 Hz,
1H), 6.73 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 5.12 (s, 2H), 4.38 (t, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H),
3.09 (t, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.5 MHz) δ 166.01, 158.22,
154.33, 147.88, 144.26, 137.01, 136.94, 128.38, 127.72, 127.41, 124.88,
124.64, 124.26, 123.90, 111.34, 104.72, 70.06, 51.23, 27.72; HRMS Calcd
for C21H19N2O2 [M+H+]: 331.1441; Found: 331.1450. 11': 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400
MHz) δ 8.62 (d, J = 4.8 Hz, 1H), 8.03 (s, 1H), 8.85-8.82 (m, 2H),
7.44-7.30 (m, 6H), 6.49 (s, 1H), 5.09 (s, 2H), 4.40 (t, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H),
2.97 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 2.28 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.5 MHz) δ
168.52, 166.29, 159.57, 154.36, 148.15, 147.04, 145.61, 137.24, 136.83,
128.65, 128.07, 127.69, 125.25, 124.31, 116.84, 105.08, 102.86, 70.56,
51.33, 25.55, 20.96; HRMS Calcd for C23H21N2O4 [M+H+]: 389.1496; Found:
389.1505.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, capped vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Improved Protocol for Indoline Synthesis via Palladium-Catalyzed
Intramolecular C(sp2)-H Amination
