$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Amination of anthra[1,9-cd: 5,10-c'd']bisisoxa zole (I). Bisisoxazole I,
0.025 mol, was added at 20-25 °C to 20 ml of dimethylacetamide. The
mixture was saturated with argon, and 2 ml of a 30% aqueous solution of
diethylamine or 2 ml of the other amine (butylamine, piperidine,
morpholine, or cyclohexylamine) was added with stirring. The mixture was
kept for 20-80 h at 20-25°C; during that time, the initial bisisoxazole I
dissolved and the solution turned violet.
7-Amino-3-dimethylamino-6H-anthra[1,9-cd]isoxazol- 6-one (Va)
crystallized from the reaction mixture and was filtered off, washed with
alcohol, and dried. The other products were isolated as follows. The
mixture was heated to 50-60°C, 5-15 ml of water was added, the mixture
was cooled to 0-5°C, and the precipitate was filtered off, dried, and
purified by column chromatography on aluminum oxide using toluene as
eluent. The solvent was removed from the eluate. Compounds Vb-Vd, VIa,
and VIb. Vb: mp: 160-162°C; Formula: C18H17N3O2. VIa: mp: 214-216°C;
Formula: C20H19N3O2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Amination of anthra[1,9-cd:5,10-c'd']bisisoxazole with alkylamines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gornostaev, L. M.; Mitrokhin, R. V.; Solov'eva, I. A.; Arnol'd, E. V.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of Organic Chemistry (Translation of Zhurnal
Organicheskoi Khimii) (2000), 36(9), 1353-1356

